WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:01.603
- It's so hot.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.343
Only the sun burns.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:17.398
- [Mark] So Valerie

00:00:17.398 --> 00:00:18.231
- Yeah.

00:00:18.231 --> 00:00:19.213
- [Mark] How long you been
down here on Skid Row?

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.677
- Wow. Got a great piece.

00:00:23.677 --> 00:00:25.015
- 20 years.

00:00:25.015 --> 00:00:27.520
- [Mark] 20 years. And where
are you from originally?

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.198
- Boyle Heights

00:00:29.198 --> 00:00:31.405
- [Mark] So East LA?

00:00:31.405 --> 00:00:36.405
- Yep. My son was, he's 22, so

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.220
- [Mark] Your son is 22?

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.433
- Mm-hm. My daughter's 32. Yeah.

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:45.961
- [Mark] And where do you sleep at night?

00:00:45.961 --> 00:00:47.700
- In a tent.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.431
- [Mark] Right here,
right down the street?

00:00:50.431 --> 00:00:51.720
- Mm-hm.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.883
- [Mark] What is your drug
of choice here on the street?

00:00:55.037 --> 00:00:56.100
- Well, she was taken cause SRLs

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.490
aren't the same for (mumble)
and I was in recovery

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:01.640
and they took my house,

00:01:02.856 --> 00:01:03.773
and my son,

00:01:04.929 --> 00:01:07.346
and my husband, everything.

00:01:07.346 --> 00:01:09.958
And I've been here ever since.

00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:11.387
- [Mark] Recovery from what?

00:01:11.387 --> 00:01:13.220
- Recovery, in recovery.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.070
- [Mark] But which drug?

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.198
- All of them, any.

00:01:16.198 --> 00:01:17.031
(laughter)

00:01:17.031 --> 00:01:18.776
- [Mark] Did you do any at all?

00:01:18.776 --> 00:01:20.196
- Not anymore.

00:01:20.196 --> 00:01:21.310
- [Mark] Which is your favorite?

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.628
- M A

00:01:22.628 --> 00:01:23.461
- [Mark] I'm sorry?

00:01:23.461 --> 00:01:25.197
- Drugs Addicts Anonymous.

00:01:25.197 --> 00:01:27.556
- [Mark] But which drugs
were your favorite?

00:01:27.556 --> 00:01:28.642
- Any of them.

00:01:28.642 --> 00:01:29.658
- [Mark] It doesn't matter?

00:01:29.658 --> 00:01:30.491
- Uh-uh.

00:01:31.495 --> 00:01:36.495
I don't use one or the
other, they all hold hands.

00:01:36.527 --> 00:01:37.957
Is that all right?

00:01:37.957 --> 00:01:39.590
- [Mark] Yes.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:41.034
- I don't use cocaine anymore.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.696
- [Mark] Why not?

00:01:42.696 --> 00:01:44.315
- 'Cause the earth starts moving.

00:01:44.315 --> 00:01:45.794
(laughter)

00:01:45.794 --> 00:01:49.440
If I take a hit, the swoosh swoosh.

00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:52.020
So I, that's...

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.563
- [Mark] And what do you do for money?

00:01:55.622 --> 00:01:59.550
- Praise God (laughing)

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.320
- [Mark] Do you pick up men sometimes?

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.048
- No. I recycle.

00:02:04.048 --> 00:02:05.338
- [Mark] You recycle?

00:02:05.338 --> 00:02:06.171
- Yeah.

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.470
- [Mark] You see your son?

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.140
- Yeah. He's in jail right now.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:11.740
- [Mark] He's in jail? What for?

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:18.150
- I don't know, but he's
supposed to be getting out soon

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.986
and he's been a lot, you know, but he's

00:02:22.986 --> 00:02:26.420
she'll be getting out and
it just, I don't know.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.780
It's kinda hot in here.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.280
- [Mark] Yeah. We'll be quick.

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:37.785
- It's a long story, you know?

00:02:37.785 --> 00:02:39.460
- [Mark] Tell me.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:42.140
- Yeah. It's 'cause when
they took my son, you know

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.970
we weren't married and recovery

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.370
he relapsed and then they
took everything from me.

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.799
So, I was in jail because
he had drugs in the house

00:02:49.799 --> 00:02:52.519
and then took my son, and
then they took all my stuff

00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:54.210
and my house

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.410
and then they put me in prison

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:58.290
and then all my stuff
got taken away from me,

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.650
so, and my son too.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:04.190
And then my husband left me
here downtown at the Wine Cart.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:06.260
So I haven't seen him ever since.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:09.010
And my son, I hadn't seen for 10 years

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.620
and he barely came

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.986
started coming to see
me when he turned 18.

00:03:13.986 --> 00:03:16.590
And then he went to jail.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.630
So, I don't know.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.600
And I've never depended on nobody.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.340
I've never had this much problems

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.650
in my life, but I've always been

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:26.850
self-supporting taking care of myself

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:30.590
you know, I don't, I don't
go with bed because I'd feel

00:03:30.590 --> 00:03:35.010
that it would to myself
demeaning that people shouldn't

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:37.973
ever think about each
other like that, you know?

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:44.200
But I can't change everyone
or anything without God, so

00:03:44.942 --> 00:03:48.050
you know, a lot of times
it's just real stressful

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:50.140
because there's really nobody to talk to.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:53.070
They really don't want
to talk about real things

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.690
because they're trying
to evade it, you know.

00:03:55.690 --> 00:03:57.250
But I said you can't evade it,

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.533
it's going to be there
in the end, you know?

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:01.910
I never cried before

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.380
and that's what almost killed me

00:04:03.380 --> 00:04:05.282
was an emotional breakdown, you know,

00:04:05.282 --> 00:04:09.575
I was only supposed serious,
get my life together

00:04:09.575 --> 00:04:11.530
you know, and have some kids

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:13.483
and someone in my life.

00:04:13.483 --> 00:04:16.437
I have to take, try to make
sure my mom would be okay

00:04:16.437 --> 00:04:18.490
'Cause he didn't have a good husband

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:20.730
and my grandma because she
didn't have one at all,

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.310
you know?

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:23.720
And then women with children,

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.650
that's how I learned
that women with children

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:26.720
other men don't want them,

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.002
and especially if they have more children

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:31.609
with different men, you know?

00:04:31.609 --> 00:04:35.943
So my grandma had three,
from three different fathers

00:04:35.943 --> 00:04:38.550
and my mom had only had one,

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:39.770
so I saw that

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:42.560
and then, so I waited
10 years to have my kids

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.577
'cause I wasn't, it's a long story.

00:04:46.554 --> 00:04:48.223
Can I've some tissue please?

00:04:48.223 --> 00:04:50.985
I'm sorry (crying)

00:04:50.985 --> 00:04:53.967
Thank-you. I apologize.

00:04:55.314 --> 00:04:56.449
- [Mark] It's okay.

00:04:56.449 --> 00:04:59.210
This is not even, this
is not even my behavior

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.947
you know, acting human, you know, but...

00:05:01.947 --> 00:05:05.620
- [Mark] It's dangerous out
here on the street, are you...

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:07.820
- Yeah. But we're all dangerous, you know,

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:12.543
especially Jesus, you know,

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:15.440
he's the one I worry about the most.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.880
I don't want to get into too much (crying)

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:28.034
Yeah, so being here, I just
try to take care of myself

00:05:28.034 --> 00:05:31.650
and do the best that I can
without getting into too much,

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:35.120
but people just don't
understand how not to steal,

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:35.953
oh my God,

00:05:35.953 --> 00:05:37.000
you shouldn't steal.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.303
He says don't steal for a reason people,

00:05:38.303 --> 00:05:39.910
you know what I mean?

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.200
Could drive some crazy, you know?

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.900
And seeing you stealing from your salary

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.547
like nobody else, you know, so.

00:05:46.547 --> 00:05:49.040
- [Mark] Did you have a job
once when you were married?

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:50.049
- Oh yeah.

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:52.053
- [Mark] What were you doing?

00:05:52.053 --> 00:05:57.053
- A receptionist. I worked
for job court typing stuff.

00:05:59.073 --> 00:06:00.393
Yeah. I had jobs.

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:04.820
I tried to work for the dog catcher

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:07.130
but I think they have spirituality rules.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.210
I didn't, I didn't know nothing

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:09.810
about spirituality 'til I got here

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.669
so I kind of dues by that, you know?

00:06:12.669 --> 00:06:17.253
Ooh it's hot. You need a fan in here too.

00:06:17.253 --> 00:06:19.063
(Laughter)

00:06:19.063 --> 00:06:21.743
Yeah, I got one too. I'll
bring it to you, okay?

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.300
But like, I don't really choose...

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:26.480
- [Mark] Well Valerie, thank-you so much

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:27.599
for talking to me.

00:06:27.599 --> 00:06:30.644
- Oh you're welcome.
I'm gonna need a bath.

00:06:30.644 --> 00:06:31.477
- [Mark] Be safe out there.

00:06:31.477 --> 00:06:32.310
- Okay, thank-you.

